  "method": [
    "Ranges with no relocatable field: every 16-byte-aligned offset of .text (every offset for ranges of 16 bytes or less), and every 8-byte-aligned offset of .rdata for the hash table, was hashed and compared with the audited digest.",
    "Ranges with relocatable fields: at each candidate place the bytes of the old build were rebuilt from the new ones by moving back the rel32 branch and RIP-relative fields (rel_old = rel_new + delta_code - delta_target), the image-relative displacements and the jump table entries (old = new - delta_target), and the rebuilt range was hashed. A match means the audited code, moved, with no other byte changed. Target deltas were taken from the proven anchors around each target; the wallet guards, whose old bytes are retained in the audit, gave the first ones directly.",
    "Vtables: searched in .rdata as the places whose slots hold the new addresses of the proven getters; the nine vtables of the routes and the item context are each referred to by exactly two lea instructions (constructor and destructor).",
    "Functions the inventory reader compares by address only were disassembled in the new file and compared with the route of inventory_reader_v3.py.",
    "The audited profiles were rewritten for the new build and checked with the audit's own check_profile_offline.py (unchanged) against the installed file."
  ],
